<!-- THE PROBLEM -->
<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="split-label">
        <span class="eyebrow">The problem</span>
        <h2>The ideas keep coming.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="split-body">
        <p>You spent a lifetime becoming the person other people ask. The philosophy, the catalog, the curriculum, the thing that took a lifetime to learn.</p>
        <p>And it keeps coming. A song idea at eleven at night. A framework you could teach in your sleep. A closet full of photographs.</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom:0">Most of it lives in your head, in your voice, on index cards. You want it out where a stranger can find it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- WHAT I DO -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="split-label">
        <h2>What I do</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="split-body">
        <p><strong>You stay the one with the ideas.</strong> You talk, I ask questions, and you correct me when I get it wrong. Your words, your judgment, your call. I run the machines.</p>
        <p><strong>Work arrives every Friday.</strong> Finished, and explained in plain words. You look it over. I keep going.</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom:0"><strong>Your organization owns all of it.</strong> Everything lands in a library with your organization’s name on it. It stacks up week after week, in one place and in order.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

